## Generate components, views and services

- `{{packageManager}} run generate <component|view|service> ELEMENT_NAME`

Supports nested paths, for example:

`{{packageManager}} run generate component path/to/my-component`

Generated elements are automatically exported from the corresponding barrel file:
`src/app/<components|views|services>/index.ts`.

## Configuration

### `nutin.config.js`

Main build and feature configuration. See the inline comments for details.

- `tailwind`, `i18n`, `inlineTemplates`, `generateSEOFiles` — top-level features.
- `generator.*` — controls what the generator scaffolds.
- `builder.*` — controls build behavior.
- `testinNutin.*` — controls TestinNutin.

### `config/seo.json`

- Register your routes' description, title and ogImage here.
- Data is used to generate static HTML per route, robots.txt and sitemap.xml.
- Unused if `nutin.config.js -> generateSEO` is disabled.

### `config/languages.json`

- Register supported languages for i18n here.
- Unused if `nutin.config.js -> i18n` is disabled.

## Register global components

If you need components to be outside of `<main>` (`<header> / <footer>`), initialize them in `main.ts`.

*Note*: `View` subclasses inherit `hideHeader()` / `revealHeader()` and `hideFooter()` / `revealFooter()`, which target the elements with the corresponding id (`#header` and `#footer`).

```ts
class App {
  private header: HeaderComponent;
  private footer: FooterComponent;

  constructor() {
    registerPipes();
    AppRouter(appRoutes);

    this.header = new HeaderComponent('body' as unknown as HTMLElement);
    this.footer = new FooterComponent('body' as unknown as HTMLElement);

    document.body.prepend(this.header.render());
    document.body.append(this.footer.render());
  }
}
```

## Add feature

Add optional features to an existing application:

```bash
nutin-add <feature>
```

Available features:
- accessibility-components
- forms
- overlays
- nutin-mixins
- docker

Convenience bundles:
```bash
nutin-add libs  # accessibility-components, forms, overlays, nutin-mixins
nutin-add all   # all available features
```

## Update Nutin

```bash
nutin-update # updates to the latest compatible minor/patch version
```

`nutin-update` uses `.nutin-meta.json` to identify Nutin-managed files and preserve application changes.

Nutin updates preserve modifications made to Nutin's source files. When changes overlap, the updater reports the affected files and lets you review them.

## Testing

You can use any testing tool you prefer for application code.

This project includes TestinNutin, Nutin's lightweight testing toolkit. Nutin itself is tested exclusively with TestinNutin, and its tests are included in the generated project so you can:
- use them as executable documentation;
- run and modify Nutin's tests when customizing the framework.

Run the tests with:

`{{packageManager}} run testin-nutin`

To use TestinNutin for application tests, enable:

```js
// nutin.config.js
testinNutin: {
  includeApp: true,
}
```

See [TestinNutin docs](https://github.com/LoisKOUNINEF/nutin/tree/main/docs/TESTING.md).

## Project structure

```
config/
  languages.json
  seo.json

src/
  app/
    components/
    services/
    views/
    routes.ts
    main.ts
  assets/
  core/   -- Nutin's core source
  libs/   -- Nutin's libraries
  styles/

tools/    -- build, development, generator and testing tools

nutin.config.js
```

